{
  "id": "ss.relic.shearing",
  "name": "Shearing eye",
  "description": "One ommatidium of ss.relic.crit's compound eye, blown up until it is the whole plate, and cut three times. The facet is the same dusky violet carapace with the same paler crown up-left so the two finds read as the same organ at two magnifications \u2014 this one builds on that one \u2014 and across it lie three coral shears, parallel, the middle one longest. Three and not one, because what the find changes is the *depth* of a cut that was already landing: one line would read as a crack in the eye, three read as the same stroke gone through. They run up-right at the angle the facet's own crown is lit from, so the light and the cuts agree.",
  "tags": [
    "relic"
  ],
  "says": ["harder"],
